  "notes": "RTINGS reviews exist (PG34WCDM, PG34WCDN, 341CQPX, G85SB, 34GS95QE, AW3425DW) but pages could not be read by the fetch tool, so no RTINGS numbers recorded. No reputable lab numbers found for LG 34GS95QE or Samsung G85SB/G85SD, and none for MO34WQC36 (pcmonitors.info Jan 2026 article is spec-only: 360Hz V-stripe RGB QD-OLED, DisplayHDR TB500, 300/1300 nits, DP 2.1 UHBR20, USB-C 18W PD, KVM, 2x3W speakers, 3yr burn-in warranty). Tom's input lag is end-to-end (10-22ms); TechSpot is processing-only (<1ms). PG34WCDM and 34GS95QE are WOLED 800R, not QD-OLED. Newer rivals as of 2026: MSI MPG 341CQR X36 and ASUS PG34WCDN (TechSpot May 2026 top picks, 360Hz), Alienware AW3426DW (Tom's reviewed; ~$800, 280Hz per TechSpot), Samsung G85SD. MO34WQC36 is the direct GIGABYTE answer to PG34WCDN/341CQR X36. GIGABYTE MO34WQC2 advantages per Tom's: widest gamut (110%+), KVM, speakers; weakness vs AW3425DW per TechSpot: HDR tuning and SDR accuracy, though it often sells cheaper ($660)."
